"Let $n\\in\\mathbb{N}$. **Clique-minor separating-pair conjecture.** There exist non-isomorphic graphs $H$ and $H'$ such that\n\n$$\n\\hom(F,H)\\ne\\hom(F,H')\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad F\\text{ contains }K_n\\text{ as a minor}.\n$$\n\nHere $K_n$ is the complete graph on $n$ vertices. The paper says that proving this conjecture for every $n$ would suffice to prove the non-isomorphism conjecture for proper minor- and union-closed families; it is left open."